.TH WHYCANT 1 2026-10-28 whycant "User Commands"
.SH NAME
whycant \- explain why a user can or cannot access a path
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B whycant
[\fIflags\fR] \fIaction\fR \fIpath\fR
.br
.B whycant completion
\fBbash\fR|\fBzsh\fR|\fBfish\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B whycant
walks the full access chain for a subject, an action and a path, the way the
kernel does: every directory on the way, symbolic links, permission bits and
POSIX ACLs, root and capabilities, mount options, immutable and append-only
attributes, sticky directories, the
.B fs.protected_*
sysctls, script interpreters and dynamic loaders, and SELinux and AppArmor
denials. It reports the first link in the chain that says no, explains why,
and prints copy-paste fixes ranked from safest to broadest.
.PP
.B whycant
is strictly read-only. It never changes files, permissions, attributes or
mounts, and it never suggests
.B chmod 777
or disabling SELinux or AppArmor.
.SH ACTIONS
.TP
.BR read ", " r
open a file for reading (needs r)
.TP
.BR write ", " w
open an existing file for writing (needs w)
.TP
.B append
open an existing file for appending (needs w; allowed on append-only files)
.TP
.BR exec ", " x ", " run
execute a file (needs x, and r for scripts; checks the interpreter or loader)
.TP
.BR list ", " ls
list a directory (needs r, and x to inspect entries)
.TP
.BR traverse ", " cd
enter a directory (needs x)
.TP
.BR create ", " mk ", " touch
create a new entry (needs w and x on the directory)
.TP
.BR delete ", " rm
delete or rename an entry (needs w and x on the directory, and sticky-bit rules)
.PP
Every directory on the way needs x.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-user " " \fIname|uid\fR
Check on behalf of this user. Without it, the user running whycant is
checked, with the groups of the current session (SUDO_USER is not used).
.TP
.BR \-g ", " \-\-group " " \fIname|gid\fR
Also assume membership of this group. Repeatable; useful for "would it work
if I add this group?".
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-pid " " \fIpid\fR
Use a running process's credentials: filesystem uid and gid, groups,
capabilities and security label. Cannot be combined with
.B \-u
or
.BR \-g .
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-all
Do not stop at the first blocker; report every problem.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Show passing checks too.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print a JSON document instead of text (schema version 1).
.TP
.B \-\-verify
Confirm the analysis with the kernel: run a probe as the subject that calls
.BR access (2),
and compare. Needs root. The probe changes nothing.
.TP
.BR \-\-color " " \fIauto|always|never\fR
When to use color. The default,
.BR auto ,
uses color on terminals unless
.B NO_COLOR
is set or
.B TERM
is
.BR dumb .
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Print only the verdict line.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show version information.
.PP
Put
.B \-\-
before a path that starts with a dash.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
access allowed
.TP
.B 1
access denied
.TP
.B 2
usage error
.TP
.B 3
could not determine: whycant itself could not inspect part of the path
(run it again with sudo)
.TP
.B 4
\-\-verify disagreed with the analysis; this is a bug,
please report it with the \-\-json output
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable color.
.TP
.BR LC_ALL ", " LC_CTYPE ", " LANG
A locale that is set but not UTF-8 makes whycant use ASCII symbols.
.TP
.B COLUMNS
Overrides the terminal width.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
whycant \-u www\-data read /srv/app/config/db.yml
whycant \-\-pid "$(pidof \-s nginx)" read /var/www/html/index.html
sudo whycant \-\-verify \-u deploy create /srv/releases/new
whycant \-\-json exec ./build.sh | jq .verdict
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR namei (1),
.BR getfacl (1),
.BR lsattr (1),
.BR findmnt (8),
.BR ausearch (8),
.BR access (2),
.BR path_resolution (7)
